{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The 20 s per-test hang budget kills xdist workers on every CI run\n\n## Symptom (pristine `origin/main` @ 6a5c88027c5, no other change applied)\n\nDefault suite, `pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.13)` — the ONLY leg that adds `--cov=rebar`:\n\n    run 32583448507 / job 97056277838: 11 failed, 16175 passed, 66 skipped in 1077.36s\n    run 32585303586 / job 97060825782: 11 failed, 16182 passed, 66 skipped in 1057.20s\n\nEvery failure is a worker death, each preceded by `[gwN] node down: Not properly terminated`:\n\n    worker 'gw2' crashed while running 'tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py::test_dropping_a_used_helpers_row_fails_loudly_instead_of_shrinking'\n    worker 'gw3' crashed while running 'tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_safe_boundary_is_not_unwrapped_in_repository_tests'\n    worker 'gw1' crashed while running 'tests/scripts/test_binding_lifecycle_grace_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_whole_tree'\n    ... 8 more, all whole-tree scanning gates ...\n\n`grep -c \"Failed: Timeout\"` = **0** in both jobs. Worker ids run gw0-gw12 under `-n 4`:\nxdist replaced each dead worker 11 times. The crashing SET is not stable between runs\n(`test_reconciler_jira_seam_clean_heldout` in one, `test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout`\nin the other), which is why it reads as flakiness.\n\nThe integration tier shows the same worker deaths (`node down: Not properly terminated` on\n3 of 4 nodes).\n\n## Root cause — CONFIRMED, reproduced deterministically\n\nCommit `6a5c88027c5` (story `bold-abeyant-indri` / 73b8-2d79-3046-44ce) lowered the per-test\nhang budget from **300 s to 20 s** in three places: `pyproject.toml:650` (`timeout = 20`, new\n`[tool.pytest.ini_options]` keys) and `_build-and-test.yml:662` + `:677`. `git blame -w -C -M`\non all three lines returns `6a5c88027c59` and nothing else.\n\n**Two facts combine.**\n\n1. **~14 legitimate tests genuinely cost more than 20 s on the runner.** The direct PARENT\n   commit `4d6c1cc835e`, same day, same runner class, same `-n 4 --dist worksteal --cov=rebar`,\n   under the OLD `--timeout=300` (run 32581500417 / job 97051623657, `16182 passed` in 906.38s,\n   zero crashes) reports in its own `--durations=25` block:\n\n       29.93s call  test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_safe_boundary_is_not_unwrapped_in_repository_tests\n       28.72s call  test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py::test_dropping_a_used_helpers_row_fails_loudly_instead_of_shrinking\n       22.97s call  test_binding_lifecycle_grace_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_whole_tree\n       22.63s call  test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py::test_main_on_real_tree_returns_zero\n       22.46s call  test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_for_owned_files\n       22.44s call  test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py::test_gate_reports_no_findings_for_owned_files\n       21.63s call  test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py::test_real_source_tree_is_clean\n       ... 20.87s, 21.24s, 21.29s, 21.42s, 18.71s, 18.76s ...\n\n   That is the crash list. The data refuting \"20 s is measured\" was in CI at the parent commit.\n   These are `call` times, so `timeout_func_only = true` does not help: the body IS the scan.\n\n2. **`timeout_method = \"thread\"` expresses an expiry as `os._exit(1)`, not as a verdict.**\n   `pytest_timeout.py:542` (`timeout_timer`) calls `os._exit(1)` from the watchdog thread,\n   killing the xdist worker process outright. Only the `signal` method reports\n   `Failed: Timeout`, via `pytest.fail()` at `pytest_timeout.py:502`. So a budget expiry inside\n   a worker can NEVER surface as `Failed: Timeout` — it surfaces as `node down` + `worker\n   crashed`. The zero `Failed: Timeout` count is a PREDICTION of this mechanism, not evidence\n   against it. Bug `albinic-agrologic-dolphin` (0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12) proved this same mechanism\n   and used `--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` as its deliberate crash-INDUCING amplifier.\n\n**Positive feedback loop:** 11 worker restarts re-pay process + coverage startup, so the suite\nruns 1057-1077 s instead of 906 s and the SURVIVING scanners move from ~16 s to 19.0-19.95 s —\nright against the wall. Each crash makes the next more likely.\n\n**Local runtime proof** (worktree off 6a5c88027c5, macOS py3.12, three discriminating arms on a\n25 s-body probe test under `-n 2 --dist worksteal`):\n\n    ARM A  repo ini (timeout=20, thread)   -> [gw0] node down: Not properly terminated\n                                              worker 'gw0' crashed while running '<probe>'\n                                              zero `Failed: Timeout`      == the CI signature\n    ARM B  same budget, --timeout-method=signal -> `Failed: Timeout (>20.0s) from pytest-timeout.`\n                                              a clean verdict, worker survives\n    ARM C  pre-73b8 --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread -> 2 passed in 25.88s\n\nArm B isolates the METHOD as what converts a timeout into a crash; Arm C isolates the BUDGET as\nwhat makes it fire at all. Coverage measured locally as a ~2x multiplier on these tests\n(2.91s -> 6.02s), which with the runner's slower cores is the rest of the gap.\n\n## Not attributable to any change in flight\n\nBoth failing runs are at headSha `6a5c88027c59d3e24d3e4269838fb3c591a64240` = pristine\n`origin/main`. Gerrit change 2098 (story 3436, compact-planner consolidation) touches only\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_*.py` + two compact tests — none of the 11 crashing tests, and\nneither config file. It is NOT implicated; main itself is broken for every change.\n\n## Root cause, part 3 — why a config-only restore cannot pass its own gate (2115 PS1)\n\nChange 2115 patchset 1 (a42a9d8d494) carried exactly the config restore planned below, and its\nown Verified run FAILED with the same crash signature. Run 32587991195's headSha is\n`6a5c88027c5` — the Gerrit Verified gate executes the WORKFLOW FILES FROM TRUSTED MAIN (the\n\"classify Verify route from trusted main\" job; reusable workflows resolve at the caller's sha),\nnot from the patchset. Job 97067339850 log line 989 shows the executed command was still\n`--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread`. pytest-timeout precedence is CLI > INI, so main's stale\nflag overrode the patchset's `timeout = 300` ini: 13x `node down`, 26x `worker crashed`,\n0x `Failed: Timeout`. The patchset's workflow edit was inert for its own run, so a fix expressed\nonly in config + workflow files can never be exercised by its own gate while main carries the\ntighter CLI flag.\n\npytest-timeout's full precedence is **MARKER > CLI > env > INI** (`_get_item_settings`,\n`pytest_timeout.py:388` — marker values first, CLI/env/ini fill only unset fields; verified\nempirically: a `@pytest.mark.timeout(60)` test sleeping 5 s PASSES under a hostile\n`--timeout=2 --timeout-method=thread`, the unmarked control dies at 2 s, and a marker applied by\na `pytest_collection_modifyitems` hook behaves identically, incl. under `-n 2 --dist worksteal`).\nSo the budget must be expressed as a MARKER from the repo's own tree to be effective from the\npatchset alone.\n\n## Plan\n\nRestore the budget to the value bug `balsamy-eloquent-iggypops` (89d5-61da-b621-47f8)\nestablished (\"300s dwarfs the slowest legitimate test\"), keep story 73b8's genuine improvement\n(the ini keys), and add the mechanism that makes the ini authoritative even under a stale CLI\nflag:\n\n1. `pyproject.toml` — `timeout = 20` -> `timeout = 300`; comment cites the measured 29.93 s\n   worst case rather than the falsified \"runs clean at 20 s\" claim.\n2. **NEW — `tests/_timeout_floor.py` + a call from `tests/conftest.py`'s\n   `pytest_collection_modifyitems`**: a hook that applies the ini budget as a\n   `pytest.mark.timeout(budget, method=<ini>, func_only=<ini>)` marker to every collected item\n   that does not already carry an explicit `timeout` marker, **but only when the effective\n   non-marker budget (CLI > PYTEST_TIMEOUT env > ini, pytest-timeout's own resolution) is\n   positive and BELOW the ini budget**. Floor semantics, not blanket: a blanket marker would\n   silently LOWER the live lanes' deliberately larger CLI budgets (external-integration\n   900/600/1800, structured-output 3600, test.yml 600, _optionality 600/300) because\n   marker > CLI; and `--timeout=0` (explicit disable, e.g. under a debugger) stays respected.\n   This is what makes the fix effective FROM THE PATCHSET ALONE on its own Verified run — and\n   it permanently closes the class \"a stale tighter CLI flag anywhere undercuts the repo's\n   measured budget\".\n3. `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` — REMOVE the now-redundant\n   `--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` from both shared-tier lanes (post-merge cleanup;\n   inert on this change's own run, correct once merged: the ini is then the single source and\n   the two lanes can never drift from it again).\n4. `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` — `_INI_BUDGET_SECS` 20 -> 300; marker-override arm\n   restructured out-of-process onto the generated-project helper with a small generated budget\n   (in-tree it would sleep past the 300 s budget); NEW out-of-process arms proving the floor\n   mechanism itself: (a) an unmarked over-budget-by-CLI test survives a hostile tighter\n   `--timeout` when the generated project carries the floor hook and a larger ini budget,\n   (b) the floor does NOT override a deliberately larger CLI budget, (c) the existing negative\n   arm still proves an unmarked hung test is killed by the ini alone.\n5. `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py` (NEW, carried from 2115 PS1) — the budget must\n   clear the measured 29.93 s worst legitimate body by 2x and stay a real guard (<= 600 s,\n   thread method).\n6. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — update the two contracts to the single-source\n   shape WITHOUT weakening them: `test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard` accepts\n   a lane with no explicit `--timeout=` ONLY because the repo ini carries\n   `timeout`/`timeout_method = \"thread\"` (asserted in the same test; lanes that do set the flag\n   must still set the thread method); `test_the_shared_tier_lanes_carry_the_ini_timeout_budget`\n   now asserts the two shared-tier lanes carry NO `--timeout=`/`--timeout-method=` flags at all\n   (drift is impossible rather than merely checked), plus the ini keys exist.\n7. `docs/local-dev-env.md` — document the 300 s value and the floor mechanism.\n\n`timeout_func_only = true` is deliberately KEPT (see prior revision; follow-up\n797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5 owns the fixture-phase gap).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `pyproject.toml`'s `[tool.pytest.ini_options].timeout` is 300; checked by\n      `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py::test_the_configured_budget_is_the_measured_one`.\n- [ ] The budget clears the measured 29.93 s worst legitimate body by 2x and remains a real\n      guard; checked by `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py`.\n- [ ] An unmarked test survives a HOSTILE tighter `--timeout` CLI flag when the ini budget is\n      larger (the floor mechanism, i.e. the fix is effective from the patchset alone); checked\n      by the new out-of-process floor arm in `test_timeout_budget.py`, and locally by a 25 s\n      probe under `-n 2 --dist worksteal --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` completing with\n      zero node-downs.\n- [ ] The floor does NOT lower a deliberately larger CLI budget (live lanes keep their\n      calibrated ceilings); checked by the new floor-is-not-a-ceiling arm.\n- [ ] A test whose body outruns the ini budget with no CLI flag is still killed by the ini\n      alone; checked by `test_an_unmarked_over_budget_test_is_killed_by_the_ini_alone`.\n- [ ] `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` still overrides everything; checked by the\n      out-of-process marker-override arm, which completes in seconds regardless of the\n      configured budget.\n- [ ] Both shared-tier lanes in `_build-and-test.yml` carry no `--timeout` flags (the ini is\n      the single source); checked by the updated\n      `test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_the_shared_tier_lanes_carry_the_ini_timeout_budget`.\n- [ ] Every CI pytest lane still has a per-test hang guard (explicit flag with thread method,\n      or the repo ini); checked by the updated\n      `test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard`.\n- [ ] The ubuntu py3.13 default-suite leg completes with zero `worker '.*' crashed` /\n      `node down` lines AND the integration tier COMPLETES (does not hang to the job cap);\n      checked on the change's own Verified run — which still executes main's stale\n      `--timeout=20`, so a green run is itself the discriminating proof of the floor.\n\n## Verification\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py \\\n           tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q\n    pytest tests/scripts -q -n 4 --dist worksteal\n    # discriminating probe: 25 s-body test under the repo config + hostile stale CLI flag\n    pytest <probe> -n 2 --dist worksteal --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread  # zero node-downs"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787422627677556001,"uuid":"00cf5e1e-051f-4867-b10e-466dc2bb3e97"}